    {
      "id": "epd213",
      "name": "E-paper display 2.13\" (SSD1680, 250x122)",
      "description": "Black-and-white e-paper (as in an e-reader): it reflects the room's light, uses power only while it changes, and keeps its picture with the power off. A refresh takes about 2 seconds (it flashes; BUSY is HIGH meanwhile), so it's for things that change now and then. SPI: SCK, MOSI (DIN), CS, DC, RST, BUSY. With #include <Adafruit_EPD.h>: Adafruit_SSD1680 display(250, 122, DC, RST, CS, -1, BUSY); display.begin(); display.clearBuffer(); display.setTextColor(EPD_BLACK); display.print(\"Hi\"); display.display();",
      "swatch": "#e8e8e2",
      "mass": 8,
